  "text": "Four billion years ago, the sun was about 30% dimmer. Earth should have frozen. It didn't. Rocks nearly that old formed underwater. The usual answer? Thicker greenhouse air holding the heat the weaker sunlight couldn't give. It's been brightening ever since. The full film, Is the Sun Getting Brighter?",
